<%# ═══════════════════════════════════ MANIFESTO ═══════════════════════════════════ %>
<section class="landing-section landing-manifesto">
  <div class="landing-inner">
    <div class="landing-section-header">
      <span class="landing-label">WHAT WE BELIEVE</span>
      <h2>A place to talk, not a product to use.</h2>
    </div>
    <div class="landing-principles">
      <div class="landing-principle">
        <h3>Familiar by design</h3>
        <p>You shouldn't have to teach your community a new app. Sabha works the way they already chat: rooms for topics, threads for tangents, search for memory. The interface stays out of the way so the conversation can be the thing.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="landing-principle">
        <h3>Small on purpose</h3>
        <p>Sabha does one thing (community chat) and refuses to do more. No marketplaces, no boost economies, no constant new features clamoring for attention. If it doesn't earn its place in your community, it doesn't ship.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="landing-principle">
        <h3>Yours, not ours</h3>
        <p>Your community runs on code you can read, on a server you can move, with data you can take. Sabha is yours from the first message. If we ever stop being useful, you walk away with everything: no negotiation, no rescue mission.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<div class="landing-divider"></div>

